### Understanding content collections

Content collections in Astro provide **type-safe** access to your content. They combine the flexibility of file-based content with the safety of TypeScript schemas.

To define a collection, create a `content.config.ts` file:

```typescript
import { defineCollection, z } from "astro:content";

const posts = defineCollection({
  schema: z.object({
    title: z.string(),
    publishedAt: z.date(),
    draft: z.boolean().default(false),
  }),
});

export const collections = { posts };
```

The schema validates your frontmatter at build time, catching errors before they reach production. Key benefits include:

1. Type inference in your templates
2. Build-time validation of content
3. Autocompletion in your editor
4. Clear documentation of content structure

> Content collections turn your content into a first-class citizen of your codebase, with all the tooling benefits that implies.

For more details, see the [official documentation](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/content-collections/).
